        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ac0cadb9a6f4737877c587bde663409",
      "statement": "In thread mode, QuickJS authenticates a persisted snapshot before an agent run when signing is configured, lazily restores its payload on the first eval, then writes a bounded snapshot and evicts the REPL slot after the run; missing or mismatched HMAC snapshots, oversized snapshots, and snapshot-creation failures are cleared.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/partners/quickjs/langchain_quickjs/middleware.py#L469-L551",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6436054b66e336060f02fd33f4b6c35c50fcb06b4dbbf000911e819ae8bcd759:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/partners/quickjs/langchain_quickjs/middleware.py#L687-L786",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d78be4d9b416b60bcb4672cc74093afc30669e360dcabe5eedd7e0a01b9fa996:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_14b5f49783a941a89136ffff644e2d83",
      "statement": "QuickJS's VM timeout does not bound wall-clock time spent in Python-hosted tool or subagent calls, and PTC and `task()` calls bypass parent ToolNode HITL enforcement; the middleware defaults to a 256-call PTC bridge budget, whose removal is explicitly unsafe for untrusted prompts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/partners/quickjs/langchain_quickjs/middleware.py#L125-L209",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0d9db34337bcd2ce22678d77acba255bb701471d72b1057c416857ac8ace3e9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13b7d06e116c49ac91eb689ce2e6d078",
      "statement": "QuickJS stores thread-mode REPL heap snapshots as a DeltaChannel patch chain, using an anchor when no smaller bsdiff patch is available; reconstruction deterministically replays anchors, patches, and clears, so persistence does not rely on an in-process cache across forks or time travel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/partners/quickjs/langchain_quickjs/_snapshot.py#L1-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6affbe198aa3ac688f7c41347b9685f68b255ef9693343365e9993843d421ca:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/partners/quickjs/langchain_quickjs/_snapshot.py#L120-L185",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cba6aa62f271bf0139b7072366960938fe779a726e5b2d4b095fb20a266ff1b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a652fdd64c154b2fbff5e98ac98ad344",
      "statement": "A QuickJS registry slot is lazily created by private slot ID and owns a dedicated worker thread, runtime, and context; runtime creation applies `SourceTransform.TOP_LEVEL_CONST_TO_VAR` for persistent top-level constants, while overlapping evaluations surface as ConcurrentEval rather than being queued.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/partners/quickjs/langchain_quickjs/_repl.py#L1001-L1114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a7e2fb6fa483c3f2b41b85bacbdfebb8e41cecc1b25099b65e82b8346261ae6:"
